I want to improve the UX of the "Ekran Kodu" field in this form.

Goal

Users often don't know where to find the screen code (e.g. MOB-001). I want to provide contextual help without cluttering the form.

Requirements
Keep the existing input field.
Add a subtle helper text below the input:

Ekran kodu, görüntülediğiniz Mercan / Omnia ekranlarında tarih bilgisinin sol kısmında yer almaktadır.

Below the helper text, add a collapsible section (accordion or expandable panel) titled:

📷 Ekran kodunun bulunduğu yeri göster

When expanded, display two image thumbnails side by side:
Mercan screen
Omnia screen
Each image should have a small caption:
Mercan ekranında konumu
Omnia ekranında konumu
Clicking an image should open it in a larger modal/lightbox so users can clearly see where the screen code is located.
Design Guidelines
Use a modern enterprise UI style similar to Atlassian, Material Design, or Ant Design.
Keep the helper text lightweight (secondary text color).
Use a subtle info icon (ℹ️) before the helper text.
The expandable section should not distract users who already know the screen code.
The form should remain clean and compact when the section is collapsed.
Use spacing and typography consistent with the rest of the form.
