UX Principles
Prioritize discoverability without increasing cognitive load.
Keep the default state minimal.
Use progressive disclosure (expand only when needed).
Ensure the layout is responsive for desktop and mobile.
Images should have rounded corners and a subtle border/shadow to match the application's design system.

Implement this as a reusable component so it can be used for other form fields that require visual guidance in the future.
